  {
    "id": "conv-linear-0001",
    "title": "Rust CLI design notes",
    "create_time": 1755000000.123456,
    "update_time": 1755003600.654321,
    "current_node": "node-08-assistant",
    "mapping": {
      "node-00-root": {
        "id": "node-00-root",
        "message": null,
        "parent": null,
        "children": ["node-01-user"]
      },
      "node-01-user": {
        "id": "node-01-user",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-01",
          "author": { "role": "user", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755000000.123456,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I'm building a Rust CLI to parse ChatGPT exports. The export loading lives at src/export/json.rs. What crate should we use for argument parsing?"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-00-root",
        "children": ["node-02-assistant"]
      },
      "node-02-assistant": {
        "id": "node-02-assistant",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-02",
          "author": { "role": "assistant", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755000060.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "clap is the standard choice for Rust CLIs. Derive-based usage looks like:\n\n```rust\nuse clap::Parser;\n\n#[derive(Parser)]\nstruct Cli {\n    #[arg(long)]\n    conversation: Option<String>,\n}\n```\n\nIt gives you `--help`, subcommands, and typed parsing for free."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-01-user",
        "children": ["node-03-user"]
      },
      "node-03-user": {
        "id": "node-03-user",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-03",
          "author": { "role": "user", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755000300.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Sounds good. We decided to use clap for argument parsing. Also see https://docs.rs/clap for the full derive reference."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-02-assistant",
        "children": ["node-04-assistant"]
      },
      "node-04-assistant": {
        "id": "node-04-assistant",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-04",
          "author": { "role": "assistant", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755000360.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Great, I'll wire that up. Anything on error handling philosophy before I start?"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-03-user",
        "children": ["node-05-user"]
      },
      "node-05-user": {
        "id": "node-05-user",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-05",
          "author": { "role": "user", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755000600.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I prefer errors over silent fallbacks. If an export is malformed, tell me about it instead of quietly guessing."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-04-assistant",
        "children": ["node-06-assistant"]
      },
      "node-06-assistant": {
        "id": "node-06-assistant",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-06",
          "author": { "role": "assistant", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755000660.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Understood. I'll surface warnings for recoverable damage — a broken parent link, a dangling current_node — and reserve hard errors for cases where no branch can be produced at all."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-05-user",
        "children": ["node-07-user"]
      },
      "node-07-user": {
        "id": "node-07-user",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-07",
          "author": { "role": "user", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755003000.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "What about the file at src/graph/branch.rs — does it already implement branch reconstruction?"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-06-assistant",
        "children": ["node-08-assistant"]
      },
      "node-08-assistant": {
        "id": "node-08-assistant",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-08",
          "author": { "role": "assistant", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755003600.654321,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Yes, src/graph/branch.rs walks up from current_node with a longest-path fallback for damaged exports. Open question: should we expose a way to pick a different strategy explicitly, or keep it fully automatic for now?"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-07-user",
        "children": []
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "conv-branch-0002",
    "title": "Regenerated answer demo",
    "create_time": 1755100000.0,
    "update_time": 1755100900.0,
    "current_node": "node-04-assistant-kept",
    "mapping": {
      "node-00-root": {
        "id": "node-00-root",
        "message": null,
        "parent": null,
        "children": ["node-01-user"]
      },
      "node-01-user": {
        "id": "node-01-user",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-b01",
          "author": { "role": "user", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755100000.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Summarize the tradeoffs between HashMap and BTreeMap for a small conversation mapping."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-00-root",
        "children": ["node-02-assistant-abandoned", "node-03-assistant-kept"]
      },
      "node-02-assistant-abandoned": {
        "id": "node-02-assistant-abandoned",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-b02",
          "author": { "role": "assistant", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755100120.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "FIRST REGENERATION (abandoned): BTreeMap is always faster for small maps because of cache locality."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-01-user",
        "children": []
      },
      "node-03-assistant-kept": {
        "id": "node-03-assistant-kept",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-b03",
          "author": { "role": "assistant", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755100240.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "SECOND REGENERATION (kept): HashMap gives O(1) average lookup and is the right default here; BTreeMap only wins if you need sorted iteration, which this mapping does not."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-01-user",
        "children": ["node-04-user-kept"]
      },
      "node-04-user-kept": {
        "id": "node-04-user-kept",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-b04",
          "author": { "role": "user", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755100500.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Good, HashMap it is. Follow-up: do we need deterministic iteration order anywhere?"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-03-assistant-kept",
        "children": ["node-04-assistant-kept"]
      },
      "node-04-assistant-kept": {
        "id": "node-04-assistant-kept",
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-b05",
          "author": { "role": "assistant", "name": null },
          "create_time": 1755100900.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Only for user-facing output like `roots()` — sort those results explicitly at the call site rather than relying on map order."
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "parent": "node-04-user-kept",
        "children": []
      }
    }
  },
